{
  "dom_id": "step-q162653",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)={e}^{t}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t\\,j+{t}^{3}\\,k.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component ${e}^{t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{ln}\u2061t$ is $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{3}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076578/assets/2e3e86e3307c4cc7f7f66772d2558fe92bd26cb808bd58263e34ea370eda00bd.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$",
